      "text": "01"
    },
    {
      "t": "h3",
      "text": "Defects reach the shopper & the feed"
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Encoding artifacts show up in SERP titles. A missing gtin blocks clean Google Merchant Center matching. A sold-out item at #3 in search is a dead end at the top of results — the kind of thing behind the BBB complaint mix (Product 15 of 50)."
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "tag": "span",
      "cls": "n",
      "text": "02"
    },
    {
      "t": "h3",
      "text": "Census → fix → prevent"
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "A full-catalog defect census, a fix-priority board weighted by price and stock, a schema patch that reaches every product at once, a sold-out policy, and a supplier price-change intake so a price file becomes a validated import — not a…"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "tag": "span",
      "cls": "n",
      "text": "03"
    },
    {
      "t": "h3",
      "text": "Double-encoded product names"
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "In a 799-item sample, 8 names carry encoding artifacts in the H1, the title tag and the JSON-LD."
    },
